    {
      "id": "0306b3b87d69efe80ba5540837989d67e740250b",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 521640083,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I was thinking we could filter this capture down to 10 or 20 packets. I know that probably isn't a realistic NetPerfMeter session, but it doesn't have to be, just the minimum needed for some functional tests.\n\nI think we could use a single DCCP stream for example. Would that work?\n\nIs it really useful to test the same dissector over different transports (if I understood correctly)?",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/jvalverde"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-04T02:21:07.966Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-04T02:21:07.966Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 90597257,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": false,
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 2264,
          "commands_changes": {}
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "24c95a127b3f4f300d02a6beff9c4232fbb0bf4d",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 521785214,
          "type": null,
          "body": "I could further reduce the size, e.g to approx. 45 KiB. Would this be okay?\n\nThe capture is used for running the \"Follow DCCP\" suite as well. Therefore, it needs multiple flows to check that it correctly identifies the flows. The \"NetPerfMeter\" suite should at least test SCTP as well as UDP, DCCP and TCP (to check that the heuristics work). NetPerfMeter over SCTP is identified by PPID, while the other protocols use the heuristics.\n\nI have an additional pull request for \"NetPerfMeter statistics\" (https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/2186), which should get some input for effective testing.\n\nI have a bit of additional work (but not ready for merge, yet), like improved DCCP sequence number presentation and statistics. This would also need additional DCCP flows for testing.",
          "author": {
            "id": 5649708,
            "username": "dreibh",
            "public_email": "dreibh@simula.no",
            "name": "Thomas Dreibholz",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/b2cd008b76724c78722d428c7836d7a098cbae94d69faf8142e43fc2445bec17?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/dreibh"
          },
          "created_at": "2021-03-04T08:29:23.306Z",
          "updated_at": "2021-03-04T08:29:23.306Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 90597257,
