      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 523359392,
          "type": null,
          "body": "@dreibh You can hold on a bit for that because this test suite needs to be refactored. We can't use tshark output (\"porcelain\") like this, otherwise it will set a precedent and small cosmetic fixes will be a nightmare to implement 3 years from now. We warn users that they can't rely on tshark's output being stable in their scripts (we do, right?), we need to do the same.\n\nI need to look at the other tests and think a bit how this should be implemented. Probably by grepping the output for `NetPerfMeterProtocol` (why not just \"NetPerMeter\" instead BTW?). Maybe count rows (frames) too. Or investigate some other output format that will be robust in the future.",
          "author": {
            "id": 2639362,
            "username": "jvalverde",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "João Valverde",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/bea5f745397cf5a2fe0526df96ec143db47f9334340ab56515038832be57e976?s=80&d=identicon",
